At last I think I have got pine working correctly again, so I'll
make a new attemt to send the complete character set ISO-8859-1
in a MIME letter in Quoted-Printable.

I'm sorry for the delay...

N.B. Because of a bug in Pine, which is in the part that parses headers,
     the From: and Reply-To: header fields can contain strange combinations
     of Â¥ and | because I have some eight bit characters in my GECOS field
     in /etc/passwd. Pine doesn't handle that. So please, check the To:
     address if you reply to this mail.

     With regards, Patrik Fältström
                         ^
                         |
                         ----This is how my swedish name is spelled!
                             Correct for the first time in Email history


